1. c4 c6 2. d4 e6 3. e4 d5 4. e5 c5 5. cxd5 cxd4 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Bb5+ Bd7 7. Bxd7+ Nxd7 8. dxe6 ! fxe6 {The critical moment. The pieces are as good as they are going to get; something has to happen now.} (8... d3 Nd2 a5 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Nf3 Nxe5 10. Nxd4 Qh4 11. Be3 Rd8 ?! 12. Qb3 Bb4+ 13. Nc3 Rxd4 14. Bxd4 Qxd4 15. Qxe6+ Ne7 16. O-O Qd6 17. Qb3 Bxc3 18. bxc3 Qb6 19. Qa4+ N5c6 20. Rab1 Qc7 21. Rfe1 Rf8 22. Qb5 g6 23. Qxb7 Qxb7 24. Rxb7 Rf4 25. g3 Ra4 26. Re2 Ra3 27. Kg2 Kf7 28. Rc7 Kf6 29. Kh3 h6 30. Kg2 Ra4 31. Rd7 Nf5 32. Rc7 Nfe7 33. Rd2 Ke6 34. Rcd7 Nf5 35. Rc7 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Nfe7 1/2-1/2
